       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 600 mg is three times the maximum recommended daily dose of sertraline, which is 200 mg/day for adults. At that dose there's a serious risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, seizures, and other toxicity. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and 70 kg weight wouldn't justify going that high.\n\nCould this be a typo? These are the usual regimens:\n- **Depression, anxiety, or OCD:** start at 25\u201350 mg once daily, then titrate by 25\u201350 mg at intervals of at least one week. The usual range is 50\u2013200 mg/day.\n- **Maximum:** 200 mg once daily.\n\nIf you meant a different dose, such as 50 mg, 100 mg, or 200 mg, tell me and I'll enter it right away. If you really do want 600 mg, for example under a specialist's direction, tell me. I'd suggest confirming with pharmacy or psychiatry first. I can then enter it with a note documenting the rationale."
      }
